---
/** Method: sources, formula, price, tests, limits. Every figure comes from params-2026.json. */
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { srcLink } from '../../lib/helpers';
import { P, SNAPSHOT } from '../../lib/engine/params';
import { OZ } from '../../lib/engine/metal';
import { breadcrumbSchema, webPageSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
import { displayDate } from '../../lib/format';
import { dec, pct, eur0, stamp } from '../../lib/money';
const lang = 'en';
const path = route('method', lang);
const title = 'Oro al Gramo method: gold price, finenesses, Spanish tax';
const description = 'How we value gold in Spain: weight times fineness times the gram price, where the price and its time come from, the legal finenesses, the savings scale, limits.';
const s = (k: string, t: string) => srcLink(k, lang, t);
const b = P.irpf.brackets;
---
<PageLayout title={title} description={description} lang={lang} jsonLd={[webPageSchema({ name: 'Method', description, path, lang }), breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: route('home', lang) }, { name: 'Method', path }])]} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Method' }]}>
  <article class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>How we work it out</h1>
    <p>Every calculator runs in your browser: nothing you type is sent or stored. Laws read in the Spanish Official Gazette on {displayDate(P.retrieved_at, 'en-GB')}.</p>
    <h2>The formula</h2>
    <p>Metal value = weight in grams × fineness ÷ 1,000 × price of a gram of pure metal. The gram price is the troy ounce price divided by {dec(OZ, 7, lang)} grams (<Fragment set:html={s('nistB9', 'NIST guide to the SI')} />). It is a metal value: a piece of jewellery can be worth more for its design or maker, and a buyer pays less because it melts, refines and takes a margin.</p>
    <h2>The price and its time</h2>
    <p>The price comes from <Fragment set:html={s('goldApi', 'gold-api.com')} />, in euros per troy ounce. It is read when the site is built (last reading: {stamp(SNAPSHOT.at.XAU, lang)}) and once more when each page opens; if that fails, the recorded price shows with its date and time. There is no continuous automatic refresh: a button lets you ask for a newer price.</p>
    <h2>The finenesses</h2>
    <p>We only use the finenesses article 9 of <Fragment set:html={s('ley17', 'Law 17/1985')} /> allows: gold {P.gold.map((g) => g.ley).join(', ')}; silver {P.silver.join(', ')}, with no tolerance below. Karat is the fineness times 24 divided by 1,000, rounded.</p>
    <h2>Tax</h2>
    <p>A gain on a sale is savings income (article 46 of <Fragment set:html={s('lirpf', 'Act 35/2006')} />), taxed at the sum of the scales in articles 66 and 76: {pct(b[0].rate, 0, lang)} up to {eur0(b[0].upTo!, lang)}, {pct(b[1].rate, 0, lang)} up to {eur0(b[1].upTo!, lang)}, {pct(b[2].rate, 0, lang)} up to {eur0(b[2].upTo!, lang)}, {pct(b[3].rate, 0, lang)} up to {eur0(b[3].upTo!, lang)} and {pct(b[4].rate, 0, lang)} above. Transfer tax is paid by the buyer (article 8 of the <Fragment set:html={s('itp', 'consolidated act')} />), at the regional rate or, failing one, {pct(P.itp.defaultMueblesRate, 0, lang)}. We do not publish each region's rate because we have not read each gazette.</p>
    <h2>Tests</h2>
    <p>The calculation engine has automated tests: one ounce of pure gold is worth exactly its price, 10 g of 750 holds 7.5 g of gold, the savings scale gives {eur0(b[0].upTo! * b[0].rate, lang)} on {eur0(b[0].upTo!, lang)}, a 995 bar is investment gold and a 990 bar is not. The site is not published if a test fails.</p>
    <h2>Limits</h2>
    <p>We do not know your piece: neither its real weight without stones nor whether the stamp is genuine. The reduction for jewellery bought before 1995 is explained, not calculated. If you spot an error, write to us from the <a href={route('contact', lang)}>contact</a> page.</p>
  </article>
</PageLayout>
